[5] Proof readout
  1. S194 reduced the full-bank route debt to 15 strict-open
     coarse ET+unit fibers containing 38 packets.
  2. On those same packets, adding first primitive safe denominator
     for 2<=q<=13 gives 30 fibers, 0 mixed route, 0 mixed status.
  3. The full primitive count deck for 2<=q<=13 gives the same
     route-pure scheduler without exact M, safe interval length, or
     topology.
  4. Ramanujan trace profiles c_q(v), 2<=q<=14, also separate the
     residual route fibers, but they are a diagnostic unless paired
     with the safe-phase inequality.
  5. Candidate theorem target: after the coarse ET+unit status gate,
     every residual Q-WITNESS row has positive primitive safe mass
     on some q<=13, while every residual COVERING-MOMENT row has zero
     such mass and must be routed by q=14/covering or by a later
     boundary-moment certificate.
